[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (INT)\nfor the check module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches pin 13 of the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pins 2,\n5, 10, 12 and 14 are earthed.</p><p>Insufficient engine oil pressure is signalled\nto pin 16 of module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from the earth signal coming from\nthe sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The ABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50 sends the &#x27;ABS\nfailure&#x27; signal to pin 8 of E30 which lights up the warning light.</strong></p><p>The ABS control unit M50 sends pin 11 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30\nthe &#x27;EBD failure&#x27; signal.</strong></p><p>The signals for the handbrake switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I40\nand brake fluid level sensor K25 both reach pin 7 of connector A\nof E10. and from there are resent to the check module E50, pin 4.</strong></p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The low brake fluid level and\nhandbrake warning light also comes on upon a command from the ABS\ncontrol unit., together with the ABS failure warning light, to indicate\na fault in the EBD braking system. \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 <a href=\"#/3234769\">E7020</a>\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</p></aside><p>If it comes on by itself, the brake fluid\nlevel is low or the handbrake is on.</p><p>For all the other warning lights, refer\nto the diagrams for the components to which they refer.</p>"]]